👋 Hey, thanks so much for making this library! Its the best slack library for rust by far. 

I changed `SlackInputBlock`'s `label` type from plain text to the existing text enum (which can be plaintext or markdown) in order to correctly add the `type` parameter. Slack API is throwing errors when the `type` field is missing for label blocks.

I confirmed that this single change will allow calls with label blocks to go through.

If you want to test this error  in block kit builder:

Not Working:
```json
{
	"type": "modal",
	"title": {
		"type": "plain_text",
		"text": "Select a Function"
	},
	"blocks": [
		{
			"type": "header",
			"text": {
				"type": "plain_text",
				"text": "Select a config"
			}
		},
		{
			"type": "input",
			"label": {
				"text": "What would you like to do?"
			},
			"element": {
				"type": "static_select",
				"placeholder": {
					"type": "plain_text",
					"text": "Select a thing"
				},
				"options": [
					{
						"text": {
							"type": "plain_text",
							"text": "Add a thing"
						},
						"value": "create"
					}
				]
			}
		}
	],
	"close": {
		"type": "plain_text",
		"text": "Test Close"
	},
	"submit": {
		"type": "plain_text",
		"text": "Test Submit"
	}
}
```


**Working:** 
```json
{
	"type": "modal",
	"title": {
		"type": "plain_text",
